    "https://cuny.jobs/85768B3D8368493E97C66F657086C5C325": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor- Accounting (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor- Accounting (Multiple Vacancies). Assistant or Associate Professor- Accounting (Multiple Vacancies) **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **\"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility** The Stan Ross Department of Accountancy is seeking applicants for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions and one tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor position in Accounting starting Fall 2027, subject to final budget approval. The successful candidates will engage in high-quality scholarly research, teach undergraduate and graduate courses in accounting, mentor students (undergraduate, masters, and Ph.D.), and share responsibility for committee and department assignments. **QUALIFICATIONS** Successful candidates must have a Ph.D. in Accounting or related fields. Candidates must also demonstrate an ability to conduct high-quality original scholarly research in accounting, the ability to teach successfully, and to cooperate with colleagues for the good of the institution. Applicants should be able to teach in multiple modalities (in-person, online, hybrid) and participate in Zicklin programs offered both on campus and with our global partners. **COMPENSATION** Assistant Professor: $205,073- $220,073 Associate Professor: $225,000- $240,000 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. **To ensure consideration, applications must be received via the official CUNY application system.** Applicants are required to submit a philosophy of teaching that includes but is not limited to their commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. Applicants are also required to submit a CV and a sample of the candidates academic writing (e.g., published papers, working papers etc) **CLOSING DATE** December 1, 2026 with review of resumes to begin September 10, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32714 Location: Baruch College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/899424D3BC19477E90C2FDD081F6116025": {
      "title": "Professor - Mathematics",
      "description": "Professor - Mathematics. Professor - Mathematics **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **\"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility** Baruch College, located in the historic Gramercy Park/Flatiron district of Manhattan, is one of eleven senior colleges of the City University of New York (CUNY), housing the Weissman School of Arts and Sciences, the Zicklin School of Business, and the Marxe School of Public and International Affairs. We are proud to serve a diverse and engaged student body of over 19,000. Our students represent a wealth of racial, ethnic, economic, religious, linguistic, and national origin backgrounds, and include many recent immigrants as well as individuals who are the first in their families to attend college. Baruch is ranked among the top institutions of higher education in the nation by The Wall Street Journal for promoting student social mobility. Baruch is also listed among the nations top public colleges for academic excellence. Baruch seeks staff and faculty members who thrive in multicultural academic environments and are committed to access and excellence in higher education. Visit us at https://www.baruch.cuny.edu/. The Department of Mathematics of Baruch College CUNY invites applications for an anticipated tenure-track position at full professor rank beginning on or about August 26, 2027. (Immediate tenure eligible only for candidates currently holding tenure at another institution of higher education in the US.) The department is seeking a candidate with at least ten years of experience in the financial sector, a strong publication record in top journals, as well as significant graduate-level teaching experience in financial engineering. The candidate must have a PhD in mathematics, applied mathematics, physics, or a related field and a scholarly record suitable for full professor rank. The department offers a world-renowned masters degree in financial engineering. At the undergraduate level, the department offer majors in financial mathematics, mathematics, actuarial science, and computer science as well as providing general education mathematics courses. **QUALIFICATIONS** The candidate must have a PhD in mathematics, applied mathematics, physics, or a related field. At least ten years of experience in the financial sector, a strong publication record in top journals, as well as significant graduate-level teaching experience in financial engineering. **COMPENSATION** $136,040- $160,827; commensurate with education and experience CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. All applications must be submitted online both at Mathjobs.org and at CUNYFirst. A complete application at MathJobs.org will include an AMS cover sheet, curriculum vitae including a list of publications, at least three letters of reference, one of which should address the candidate's teaching, short statements describing teaching philosophy and future research plans. In addition, applicants should submit a narrative statement describing their commitment to working effectively with faculty, staff, and students in a multicultural/multiethnic urban campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. The application at CUNY First will include candidates curriculum vitae, answers to screening and self identification questions, and an agreement to terms and conditions. Emailed or hard copy applications will not be considered. If you have any questions, please contact HR at 646-660-6590. **Application Materials Required:** Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: + AMS Cover sheet + Curriculum Vitae (including a list of publications) + Research Statement + Teaching Statement + Multicultural Statement + Three or More Reference Letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on Mathjobs.org) and anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: http://www.baruch.cuny.edu/math/ Prof. Warren Gordon Baruch College One Bernard Baruch Way, Box B6-230 New York, NY 10010 **CLOSING DATE** November 1, 2026 with review of resumes to begin October 1, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32733 Location: Baruch College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/33A402692C634102827DF0839656799925": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Accounting",
      "description": "Lecturer - Accounting. Lecturer - Accounting **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **\"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility** The Stan Ross Department of Accountancy is seeking applicants for one lecturer position in Accounting starting Fall 2027, subject to final budget approval. The successful candidate will primarily teach undergraduate and graduate courses in accounting. Additionally, the successful candidate is expected to mentor students (undergraduate and masters students) and undertake significant service to the department. **QUALIFICATIONS** Bachelors degree plus significant professional experience **or** Masters degree required in accounting or a related field. Demonstrate an ability and commitment to deliver high-quality teaching in accounting, auditing or taxation. Prior professional work experience in these fields and professional certification (e.g., CPA) are a plus. Successful candidates will be required to participate in Baruchs Inclusive Pedagogy workshop and CUNYs Innovative Teaching Academy, and demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching in a diverse and inclusive environment. Applicants must be able to teach in multiple modalities (in-person, online, hybrid) and participate in Zicklin programs offered both on campus and with our global partners. **COMPENSATION** $92,359- $106,547; salary commensurate with education and experience CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. **To ensure consideration, applications must be received via the official CUNY application system.** Candidates should provide a CV/resume. Applicants are required to submit a philosophy of teaching that includes but is not limited to their commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. **CLOSING DATE** December 1, 2026 with review of resumes to begin September 15, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32729 Location: Baruch College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/617BE724C81344AFB32E5AAC46BAC3DD25": {
      "title": "Lecturer Doctoral Schedule - Mathematics",
      "description": "Lecturer Doctoral Schedule - Mathematics. Lecturer Doctoral Schedule - Mathematics **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **\"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility** Baruch College, located in the historic Gramercy Park/Flatiron district of Manhattan, is one of eleven senior colleges of the City University of New York (CUNY), housing the Zicklin School of Business, the Weissman School of Arts and Sciences, and the Marxe School of Public and International Affairs. We are proud to serve a diverse and engaged student body of over 19,000. Our students represent a wealth of racial, ethnic, economic, religious, linguistic, and national origin backgrounds, and include many recent immigrants as well as individuals who are the first in their families to attend college. Baruch is ranked among the top institutions of higher education in the nation by The Chronicle of Higher Education for promoting student social mobility. Baruch is also listed among the nations top public colleges for academic excellence. Baruch seeks staff and faculty members who thrive in multicultural academic environments and are committed to access and excellence in higher education. Visit us at https://www.baruch.cuny.edu/. The Department offers undergraduate majors in Mathematics, Financial Mathematics, Computer Science, and Actuarial Science. The position includes significant instructional responsibilities. The successful candidate should be a math pedagogue, with expertise in teaching lower-division mathematics courses, and will be hired specifically to teach and potentially provide leadership for first-year mathematics courses, including Algebra, Precalculus, and Calculus. Additional responsibilities may include student advising; course and curriculum development; preparation of assessments, program reviews, and collaborative learning activities; participate in faculty and professional development initiatives; evaluation and implementation of innovative methodologies, teaching strategies, and instructional delivery methods; development of teaching materials to enhance student learning and support course objectives; assessment of student learning outcomes; and active participation in departmental, college, and university service activities. **QUALIFICATIONS** The applicant must have a Ph.D. in mathematics or equivalent, college level teaching experience; demonstrated involvement in curriculum development and experience developing innovative learning materials; demonstrated innovation in the classroom, and implementation of creative and engaging teaching strategies, such as the flipped classroom. **COMPENSATION** $93,080- $104,567; commensurate with education and experience CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. **All applications must be submitted online both at Mathjobs.org and at CUNYFirst.** The completed application at CUNYFirst will include candidates curriculum vitae, answers to screening and self-identification questions, and an agreement to terms and conditions. A complete application at MathJobs will include an AMS cover sheet, curriculum vitae, at least three letters of reference, which should address the candidate's teaching, a short statement describing teaching philosophy and future scholarship plans. In addition, applicants should submit a narrative statement describing their commitment to working effectively with faculty, staff, and students in a multicultural/multiethnic urban campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. Emailed or hard copy applications will not be considered. If you have any questions, please contact HR at 646-660-6590. Application Materials Required at Mathjobs.org: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: + AMS Cover sheet + Curriculum Vitae + Teaching Statement + Multicultural Statement + Three or More Reference Letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers at this site) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: http://www.baruch.cuny.edu/math/ Prof. Warren Gordon Baruch College, One Bernard Baruch Way, Box B6-230 New York, NY 10010 **CLOSING DATE** December 15, 2026 with review of resumes to begin immediately. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32741 Location: Baruch College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/4A5D5BA9F5DF41368BB5052B88433B5925": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Natural Sciences/Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor- Natural Sciences/Biology. Assistant Professor- Natural Sciences/Biology **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **\"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility** The Department of Natural Sciences at Baruch College, City University of New York, invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Biology, starting August 26, 2027. The candidate is expected to establish an externally funded research program that will complement the collaborative, interdisciplinary environment in the department and provide research opportunities for undergraduate students. We are seeking a candidate with excellent teaching experience and research in any area of molecular or cellular biology or genetics. The candidate would be expected to teach Molecular and Cellular Biology and develop a new course in their specialty. The Department of Natural Sciences offers general education courses for non-majors as well as majors in Biological Sciences (over 300 students), Environmental Science, and Environmental Studies, and minors in Chemistry, Environmental Sustainability, and Physics. Baruch College is in the vibrant Gramercy Park District of Manhattan. It is easily reached from the other boroughs of New York City, Westchester County, and New Jersey by car and public transportation. Its buildings include the 1929 Field Building and the modern Newman Vertical Campus completed in 2001. The College is nationally recognized for Academic Excellence, Access and Value, and Social Mobility for Students. For more information about the College, the Weissman School of Arts and Sciences, and the Department, visit the Baruch website: https://www.baruch.cuny.edu/ Baruch College is strongly committed to a diverse work environment. Our student body is one of the most diverse in the nation, bringing an unparalleled breadth of cultural experience to the campus that enriches teaching, scholarship, and student life. A vibrant and pluralistic community is fundamental to the exchange of ideas and production of knowledge. Ensuring such plurality and diversity in the faculty is fostered by active efforts in recruitment and retention and in the sustaining of a climate of openness and participation throughout the life of the College. **QUALIFICATIONS** Ph.D. degree in Molecular Biology/Genetics/Biology or a closely related field is required by August 26, 2027, when the appointment begins. We welcome applicants whose expertise complements or extends the research programs available in the department. Competitive applicants will have a strong record of peer-reviewed publications in their field, a plan to obtain external funding, promise of teaching excellence, and a commitment to mentoring undergraduate researchers. Postdoctoral experience is a plus. **COMPENSATION** $98,231- $112,841; Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. To be considered for this position, applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV) or resume, a research statement outlining plans for securing external funding and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students (maximum 3 pages), a teaching statement (maximum 3 pages), and contact information for three to five professional references, who may be contacted at a later date. Applicants are also required to submit a narrative statement (maximum 1 page) describing their commitment to and experience with working effectively with faculty and staff, and teaching students in a pluralistic urban campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first generation of their family to attend a college or university. **CLOSING DATE** November 9, 2026. Review of applications to begin October 19, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32757 Location: Baruch College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/3168BC83E11A472BA7FBA85E6D8A8C4725": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Fine and Performing Arts (Music/Music Theory)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor- Fine and Performing Arts (Music/Music Theory). Assistant Professor- Fine and Performing Arts (Music/Music Theory) **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility\"** Baruch College, one of eleven senior colleges of the City University of New York (CUNY), proudly serves a diverse and engaged student body of over 19,000. Our students represent a wealth of cultural and economic backgrounds, and include many recent immigrants as well as individuals who are the first in their families to attend college. Baruch is ranked among the top institutions of higher education in the nation by The Chronicle of Higher Education for promoting student social mobility. Baruch is also listed among the nations top public colleges for academic excellence. Baruch seeks faculty who thrive in multicultural academic environments and are committed to access and excellence in higher education. Visit us at https://www.baruch.cuny.edu/ The music program at Baruch College, CUNY, seeks a promising scholar of demonstrated scholarship or achievement and dedicated teacher, currently completing or having recently attained the Ph.D. in Music Theory, for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning Fall 2027. All degree requirements must be met by the beginning of the 20272028 academic year. The faculty member will teach a variety courses primarily in music theory to a diverse community that includes music majors and music minors. Other responsibilities may include directing independent undergraduate projects, advisement, and the like. The successful candidate is expected to conduct a scholarly agenda with significant peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations, and to engage in other activities within the profession. The faculty member will be an active participant in departmental and college-level committees and will share responsibility for academic governance, which may include curricular development and program review. **QUALIFICATIONS** Must currently be completing or having recently attained the Ph.D. in Music Theory, for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning Fall 2027. All degree requirements must be met by the beginning of the 20272028 academic year. **COMPENSATION** $89,777- $105,588; commensurate with qualifications and experience CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Applicants are required to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae and a philosophy of teaching that includes but is not limited to their commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. Candidates who are selected to be interviewed will be asked to provide additional materials. **CLOSING DATE** December 18, 2026. Review of applications to begin on December 26, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32794 Location: Baruch College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/28A807C59C8143BC87BFB6EB1704F73525": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor- Economics",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor- Economics. Assistant or Associate Professor- Economics **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility\"** Located in the historic Gramercy Park/Flatiron district of Manhattan, Baruch College serves a diverse student population that speaks more than 110 languages. Baruch is consistently ranked among the top public schools in the northeast and among the top Best Bang for the Buck colleges. The Bert W. Wasserman Department of Economics and Finance is seeking applicants for one tenure track Associate/Assistant Professor position in Economics starting Fall 2027, subject to final budget approval. The successful candidate will engage in high-quality scholarly research in economics, teach undergraduate and graduate courses in economics, mentor students (undergraduate, master's, Ph.D.), and share responsibility for committee and department assignments. Applicants should be able to teach in multiple modalities (in-person, online, hybrid) and participate in Zicklin programs offered both on campus and with our global partners. **QUALIFICATIONS** Ph.D. in Economics or a closely related field. Demonstrated ability to conduct high quality scholarly research, ability to teach successfully and to cooperate with colleagues for the good of the institution. Preference will be given to candidates specialized in computational methods used in macroeconomics and econometrics, among others. **COMPENSATION** Assistant Professor: $135,000-$150,000 Associate Professor: $171,300-$186,300 Salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. For full consideration, please complete the online application and submit a cover letter, CV, research paper(s), and a list of three references, including their contact information. Recommendation letters should be submitted to **ecofinRecruiting@baruch.cuny.edu with subject Econ Position 2026-27** . Applicants are required to submit a philosophy of teaching that includes but is not limited to their commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. **CLOSING DATE** March 15, 2027. To ensure consideration, applications must be received by December 2, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32871 Location: Baruch College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/9C92092602094995AF1CD628B2DD205E25": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor- Finance (Multiple Positions)",
