    "https://cuny.jobs/4C91B436B28A466B88B302FE40C5D5D325": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Statistics",
      "description": "Lecturer - Statistics. Lecturer - Statistics **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility\"** The Zicklin School of Business at Baruch College, City University of New York is seeking applicants for a full-time Lecturer in Statistics in the Paul H. Chook Department of Information Systems and Statistics. Preference will be given to applicants who can teach a variety of undergraduate and graduate courses in the statistics area, including, but not limited to, applied/business statistics, regression and forecasting models, data analytics, machine learning, probability, inference and other courses in Statistics. Applicants should be able to teach in multiple modalities (in-person, online, hybrid) and participate in Zicklin programs offered both on campus and with our global partners. The largest accredited collegiate school of business in the United States, Baruch College's Zicklin School of Business has earned a national and international reputation for excellence. It offers nationally ranked undergraduate, part-time, and full-time MBA programs, specialized masters, and doctoral programs. The Paul H. Chook Department of Information Systems and Statistics offers undergraduate majors and minors in Information Systems (IS) and in Statistics and Quantitative Modeling (SQM). It also offers four specialized MS degrees in IS, Business Analytics, Statistics, and Quantitative Methods & Modeling, as well as a PhD program in IS. It also provides courses for our MBA program. **QUALIFICATIONS** Candidates must have at least a masters degree in statistics or related areas. They must also demonstrate effectiveness in teaching and other faculty-related service (such as curriculum design, industry engagement, and grant work) **Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of appointment. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship.** **COMPENSATION** $92,359- $106,547 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** From our job posting system, select \"Apply Now\", create or log in to a user account, and provide the requested information. If you are viewing this posting from outside our system, access the employment page on our web site and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Applicants must provide a cover letter, a current CV, a personal statement (focusing on teaching and service), names of three references (letters to be provided if selected for the next stage), and student course evaluations if available. Applicants are required to submit a philosophy of teaching (as a part of their personal statement) that includes but is not limited to their commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. **CLOSING DATE** May 31, 2027 with review of resumes to begin on November 1, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32926 Location: Baruch College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/46BAF011377644EEB754542D55B982B625": {
      "title": "Lecturer- Information Systems",
      "description": "Lecturer- Information Systems. Lecturer- Information Systems **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility\"** The Zicklin School of Business at Baruch College, City University of New York is seeking applicants for a full-time Lecturer in Information Systems in the Paul H. Chook Department of Information Systems and Statistics. Preference will be given to applicants who can teach various courses in the department, including, but not limited to, the following areas: Cybersecurity & Information Assurance, Data Analytics and Artificial Intelligence, as well as other traditional courses in Information Systems such as Systems Analysis and Development, Programming, Cloud Computing, and Web Applications Development. Applicants should be able to teach in multiple modalities (in-person, online, hybrid) and participate in Zicklin programs offered both on campus and with our global partners. The largest accredited collegiate school of business in the United States, Baruch College's Zicklin School of Business has earned a national and international reputation for excellence. It offers nationally ranked undergraduate, part-time, and full-time MBA programs, specialized masters, and doctoral programs. The Paul H. Chook Department of Information Systems and Statistics offers undergraduate majors and minors in Information Systems (IS) and in Statistics and Quantitative Modeling (SQM). It also offers four specialized MS degrees in IS, Business Analytics, Statistics, and Quantitative Methods & Modeling, as well as a PhD program in IS. It also provides courses for our MBA program. **QUALIFICATIONS** Candidates must have at least a masters degree in information systems or related areas. They must also demonstrate effectiveness in teaching and other faculty-related service (such as curriculum design, industry engagement, and grant work). **Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of appointment. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship.** **COMPENSATION** $92,359- $106,547 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** From our job posting system, select \"Apply Now\", create or log in to a user account, and provide the requested information. If you are viewing this posting from outside our system, access the employment page on our web site and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Applicants must provide a cover letter, a current CV, a personal statement (focusing on teaching and service), names of three references (letters to be provided if selected for the next stage), and student course evaluations if available. Applicants are required to submit a philosophy of teaching (as a part of their personal statement) that includes but is not limited to their commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. **CLOSING DATE** May 31, 2027 with review of resumes to begin on November 1, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32925 Location: Baruch College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/D079EAF2BE1241239C09909240FBD78C25": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Information Systems",
      "description": "Assistant Professor- Information Systems. Assistant Professor- Information Systems **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **\"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility** The Zicklin School of Business at Baruch College, City University of New York, is seeking applicants for a full-time tenure-track faculty position in Information Systems (IS) in the Paul H. Chook Department of Information Systems and Statistics. The position is open only at the Assistant Professor level and begins in the Fall 2027 semester. Preference will be given to applicants who conduct cybersecurity research and/or can teach cybersecurity courses. The department's IS division is highly ranked in research productivity in top journals (24th nationwide in 2024 based on publications at MISQ, ISR, JAIS and JMIS over the last three years). The largest accredited collegiate school of business in the United States, Baruch College's Zicklin School of Business has earned a national and international reputation for excellence. It offers nationally ranked undergraduate, part-time, and full-time MBA programs, specialized masters, and doctoral programs. The Paul H. Chook Department of Information Systems and Statistics offers undergraduate majors and minors in Information Systems (IS) and in Statistics and Quantitative Modeling (SQM). It also offers four specialized MS degrees in IS, AI and Business Analytics, Statistics, Quantitative Methods & Modeling, along with a PhD program in IS. It also provides courses for our MBA program. **QUALIFICATIONS** Applicants must either have or expect completion of Ph.D. in Information Systems or related fields. They should have a proven record or the potential for high-quality scholarly research leading to publications in premier peer-reviewed journals in Information Systems. They must be able to teach various courses in the department, including, but not limited to, cybersecurity, information assurance, ethical hacking, systems analysis and design, and programming, among others. Applicants should be able to teach in multiple modalities (in-person, online, hybrid) and participate in Zicklin programs offered both on campus and with our global partners. Preference will be given to applicants who conduct cybersecurity research and/or can teach cybersecurity courses **COMPENSATION** $147,300- $162,300; salary commensurate with education and experience CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** To apply, go to www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Applicants must provide a cover letter, a current CV, a sample research paper, names of three references (with letters to be submitted at a later stage), and student course evaluations if available. Applicants are required to submit a philosophy of teaching that includes but is not limited to their commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. **CLOSING DATE** Open until filled. Review of applications will begin on July 1, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32329 Location: Baruch College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/ABB95D223385407AAB1E631DDC94E40225": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Human Resource Management/ Organizational Behavior",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Human Resource Management/ Organizational Behavior. Assistant Professor in Human Resource Management/ Organizational Behavior **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **\"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility** Baruch College, one of 11 senior colleges of the City University of New York, attracts motivated students of proven achievement. It is one of the most culturally diverse institutions of higher education in the United States. The Zicklin School of Business, the largest AACSB-accredited business school in the United States, offers an array of full-time, part-time, executive, and honors programs leading to BBA, MBA, MS, and PhD degrees. The Narendra Loomba Department of Management includes a faculty group of approximately 100 full-time and part-time faculty involved in teaching and research related to an array of subject matter areas. These areas include a) Human Resource Management and Organizational Behavior; b) Business, Society, and Sustainability; c) Operations Management; d) Strategic Management; and e) Business Consulting. The Narendra Paul Loomba Department of Management at the Zicklin School of Business is pleased to invite applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Human Resource Management / Organizational Behavior, commencing in August 2027, subject to final budget approval. **QUALIFICATIONS** We seek applicants who hold a PhD (or are ABD) in Human Resource Management, Organizational Behavior, Industrial-Organizational Psychology, or a related field. The successful candidate will demonstrate an established record of peer-reviewed scholarly publication and the capacity to sustain a rigorous research agenda targeting top-tier outlets, including those on the UTD24 and FT50 lists. Candidates must have a proven record of teaching Human Resource Management or Organizational Behavior courses at undergraduate and graduate levels. Experience in teaching courses in Human Resource Management is beneficial but not required. Applicants should be able to teach in multiple modalities (in-person, online, hybrid) and participate in Zicklin programs offered both on campus and with our global partners. In addition, interest in contributing to student mentorship and advisement are desired. **COMPENSATION** $169,000- $184,700; commensurate with qualifications and experience CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** To apply, go to www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Applicants should include a CV; a research statement; a teaching statement; a statement about contributing to a pluralistic, urban environment; copies of recent publications; at least 3 recommendation letters (applicants will be asked to provide contact details of their recommenders, who will be contacted by the system and instructed on how to submit their recommendation letters); and a summary of recent teaching evaluations if available. **Emailed or hard copy applications will not be considered.** Applicants are required to submit a research statement and a philosophy of teaching that includes but is not limited to their commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. For any questions, please contact Matthew Perrigino (matthew.perrigino@baruch.cuny.edu). **CLOSING DATE** November 16, 2026 With review of resumes to begin October 1, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32496 Location: Baruch College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/8C0FF6715A1B48FF9EC62B43204EF5D025": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Strategic Management",
      "description": "Assistant Professor- Strategic Management. Assistant Professor- Strategic Management **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **\"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility** Baruch College, a senior college of the City University of New York (CUNY), is located in the historic Gramercy/Flatiron district between Midtown and Lower Manhattan. This prime location offers significant professional opportunities to interact with operations, supply chain, and analytics professionals across various sectors, including healthcare, retail, banking and finance, technology, transportation, and government. The Zicklin School of Business, New York Citys premier public business school, is renowned for its excellence in offering nationally ranked business programs. These include BBA and MBA degrees; specialized MS degrees; executive programs; and the Zicklin PhD in Business (which includes a specialization in Management & Entrepreneurship) offered jointly with the CUNY Graduate Center. The Strategy faculty routinely publish in top-tier journals and host internationally-known scholars in the departments research seminar series. The Narendra Paul Loomba Department of Management at the Zicklin School of Business is pleased to invite applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Strategic Management, commencing in August 2027, subject to final budget approval. **QUALIFICATIONS** We seek applicants who hold a PhD (or are ABD) in Strategic Management or a closely related field. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain a rigorous research agenda in strategic management, leading to publications in top-tier journals such as Strategic Management Journal, Organization Science, and Journal of International Business Studies, as well as contribute to the doctoral concentration in Management & Entrepreneurship. We especially welcome applicants conducting research with an emphasis on global contexts and/or strategy analytics. Junior faculty in the strategic management area typically teach BBA courses in strategic management. More senior faculty (i.e., senior assistant professor and higher) are expected to contribute to the Zicklin Schools growing catalog of courses at the MBA and MS levels and to support the growth initiatives for the BBA in Management. Applicants should be able to teach in multiple modalities (in-person, online, hybrid) and participate in Zicklin programs offered both on campus and with our global partners. **COMPENSATION** $163,000- $178,500; commensurate with qualifications and experience CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** To apply, go to www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Applicants should include a CV; a research statement; a teaching statement that includes but is not limited to commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university; copies of recent publications; at least 3 recommendation letters (applicants will be asked to provide contact details of their recommenders, who will be contacted by the system and instructed on how to submit their recommendation letters); and a summary of recent teaching evaluations if available. **Emailed or hard copy applications will not be considered.** Members of the faculty will attend the Academy of Management Annual Meeting July 31st to August 4th, 2026 in Philadelphia, PA, and the Strategic Management Society Annual Conference October 17-20, in Berlin, Germany. Job market candidates who will be presenting at either of these conferences are encouraged to submit a cover letter and vita to MGT-Recruiting@baruch.cuny.edu **(documents submitted by e-mail are not a substitute for an applicationall applications must be submitted via the CUNY application system.)** **CLOSING DATE** November 16, 2026. Applicants should submit their full applications as soon as possible. Review of applications will begin after October 1, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32535 Location: Baruch College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/F8CD4A7ABA3A49A5B0C2048C6431D24F25": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor- Higher Education Administration",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor- Higher Education Administration. Assistant or Associate Professor- Higher Education Administration **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **\"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility** The Austin W. Marxe School of Public and International Affairs at Baruch College invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant or tenured Associate Professor of Higher Education Administration, beginning in August 2027. The position requires teaching across the MSEd and EdD in Higher Education Administration. The candidate will also be expected to chair dissertation-in-practice committees and mentor doctoral students. The Marxe School values a faculty which represents diverse viewpoints and backgrounds and is committed to building an inclusive academic community. For more information on the values and priorities of the school, please see our mission statement and strategic plan posted at https://marxe.baruch.cuny.edu/about/ **QUALIFICATIONS** Candidates must hold a PhD or other doctorate in higher education, higher education administration, educational leadership, or a closely related field or be on schedule for dissertation defense by Summer 2027. The candidate must have completed a doctorate prior to the teaching start date for the Fall 2027 semester. Experience chairing doctoral committees is preferred. The search committee seeks candidates who maintain an active program of scholarly research in higher education or a closely related field. We are especially interested in candidates whose work draws on critical methodologies suited to practitioner-scholar doctoral research, including critical quantitative methods; policy analysis, case study methods, participatory action research, or community-based participatory research; or critical qualitative and narrative research. We will give special consideration to candidates who have chaired Doctor of Education (EdD) or equivalent doctoral dissertation committees and who have helped develop or refine EdD curriculum. The ideal candidate brings a record of expanding access to postsecondary education and to advancing educational justice, demonstrated through a combination of research, teaching, mentoring, and service. **COMPENSATION** Assistant Level: $94,909 - $102,017 Associate Level: $98,995- $105,816 CUNY is in the process of implementing salary schedule increases. Once implemented, salaries of eligible employees will be adjusted by 3.5% effective 9/1/26, in accordance with the terms of the PSC-CUNY collective bargaining agreement. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. All items to be uploaded must be combined in a single document. If you are viewing this posting from outside our system, access the employment page on our web site and search for this vacancy using the Job ID provided. Candidates should submit in PDF format a CV, statement of research interests, statement of teaching philosophy, a representative paper or publication, and a cover letter addressed to the committee chair, Professor Ryan Coughlan. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe the candidates commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. The cover letter should be structured around the following four prompts: 1. Describe how your research, teaching, and service align with Baruchs leadership in social and economic mobility and the Marxe Schools public mission. 2. Describe your experience with practitioner-scholar doctoral education, including chairing dissertations-in-practice or equivalent committees and contributing to Doctor of Education (EdD) curriculum. 3. Describe your applied and critical methodological commitments, and how they prepare you to teach research methods and mentor doctoral students conducting dissertations-in-practice. 4. Describe your record of contributing to the expansion of access to postsecondary education and the advancement of educational justice through any combination of research, teaching, mentoring, and service **CLOSING DATE** December 8, 2026 Review of resumes to begin October 5, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32553 Location: Baruch College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/DF285CB27FE4496AB3A8DED80600E1EA25": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor- Real Estate",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor- Real Estate. Assistant or Associate Professor- Real Estate **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **\"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility** The William Newman Department of Real Estate at Baruch College, City University of New York (CUNY), invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor position beginning in Fall 2027. We seek candidates with a strong commitment to scholarly research, excellence in teaching, and active engagement in a dynamic real estate program. The Department offers undergraduate and graduate degree programs and maintains strong connections with the real estate industry through its location in New York City and its affiliation with the Steven L. Newman Real Estate Institute. Baruch College, located in Manhattans historic Gramercy Park and Flatiron districts, provides access to the nations largest real estate market, major financial institutions, leading real estate firms, and a vibrant network of industry professionals. The Colleges more than 19,000 students, who speak over 110 languages, have been repeatedly recognized as among the most diverse student populations in the United States. The successful candidate will be expected to maintain an active research agenda leading to publications in leading academic journals, teach undergraduate and graduate courses in real estate and related areas across multiple instructional modalities (in-person, online, and hybrid), contribute to the Departments academic and professional activities, and support the Schools growing portfolio of global and executive education programs. We welcome applications from candidates in all areas of real estate research. **QUALIFICATIONS** Applicants must possess a Ph.D. in Real Estate, Finance, Economics, or a closely related discipline by the date of appointment. Successful candidates will demonstrate the ability to conduct high-quality scholarly research and publication, a commitment to excellence in teaching, and a willingness to contribute actively to the Departments academic and professional initiatives. Applicants at the Associate Professor level should have an established record of scholarly achievement and demonstrated potential for leadership in research, teaching, and service. **COMPENSATION** $220,000- $235,000; commensurate with qualifications and experience The Department and College offer a supportive research environment, including access to major financial and real estate databases and research support resources. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** From our job posting system, select \"Apply Now\", create or log in to a user account, and provide the requested information. If you are viewing this posting from outside our system, access the employment page on our web site and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Applicants are required to submit a CV and contact information for recommendation letters. Applicants are required to submit a research statement and a philosophy of teaching that includes but is not limited to their commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university **CLOSING DATE** December 8, 2026. To ensure full consideration, applications should be received by October 30, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32495 Location: Baruch College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/19E98B72655C40D3B5C854FA0C8CE4B025": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Sociology of Gender and Sexuality",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Sociology of Gender and Sexuality. Assistant Professor - Sociology of Gender and Sexuality **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **\"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility** The Sociology and Anthropology Department at Baruch College, a senior college of the City University of New York located in the heart of mid-town Manhattan, invites applications for a sociologist with a specialization in gender and sexuality for a full-time assistant professor position to begin August 28, 2027. The department, which is housed in the college's Weissman School of Arts and Sciences, has a multidisciplinary faculty and supports degrees in Sociology, Anthropology, Religion, and New York City Studies. The school serves all Baruch students in its introductory courses, many minors in its upper-level courses, and an increasing number of majors. Baruch College is especially interested in candidates who can contribute to its mission of educating one of the most diverse student bodies in the United States. The successful candidate will have a strong scholarly research agenda and demonstrate preparation to teach in department courses that include introduction to sociology, upper-level courses in gender and sexuality studies, and other courses as needed in the departments curriculum. Evidence of ability to engage students in experiential, community-oriented learning and in New York City-based learning is desired. **QUALIFICATIONS** + Doctoral degree in sociology with specialization in gender and/or sexuality. + Demonstrated successful experience teaching courses in sociology at the college level. Candidates will be expected to demonstrate: + Excellence in scholarship, including publication (or a publication trajectory) in respected outlets + Teaching excellence, including course and assignment design, and ability to teach a diverse student body using a variety of modalities + Ability to engage students in experiential learning and community-based learning + Engagement in service to the university and broader discipline of sociology **COMPENSATION** $86,741- $102,017; commensurate with education and experience CUNY is in the process of implementing salary schedule increases. Once implemented, salaries of eligible employees will be adjusted by 3.5% effective 9/1/26, in accordance with the terms of the PSC-CUNY collective bargaining agreement. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** To apply, go to www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Qualified applicants should submit the following materials: + A cover letter explaining the candidates qualifications for the position and specifying the upper-level courses they would be interested in teaching + A curriculum vitae + A 1-2 page research statement describing the content and significance of current and future projects + A 1-2 page statement of teaching philosophy, including but not limited to the candidates commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. + The names of three references **Please Note: Emailed or hard copy applications will not be considered.** Candidates who are selected to be interviewed will be asked to provide the following additional materials: + 3 letters of recommendation + Evidence of effective teaching as demonstrated through sample course materials, student evaluations, and/or peer observation reports **CLOSING DATE** November 30, 2026; review of applications to begin on December 1, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32564 Location: Baruch College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/A7EFBCDAD90C40CAA0D58172809056CB25": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Law (Sustainability)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor- Law (Sustainability). Assistant Professor- Law (Sustainability) **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** **\"At Baruch College we believe that student success is everyones responsibility** The Zicklin School of Business of Baruch College/CUNY invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position in the Department of Law at the Assistant Professor level, with a focus on environmental law and sustainability. The Department of Law offers courses to undergraduate and graduate business students in a wide variety of business subjects, including Introduction to Business Law, Business Organizations, and an array of upper-level specialty courses, including Law, Business and Sustainability, Environmental Law, Financial Technology (Fintech), Financial Regulation, Artificial Intelligence (AI), Immigration Law and Law and Legal Theory. The Zicklin School of Business is accredited by AACSB International, and is among the largest schools of business in the U.S. Baruch College is located in Manhattans historic Gramercy/Flatiron district between Midtown and Wall Street and offers significant professional opportunities to interact with the legal, banking and finance, technology, and government sectors. The Zicklin School of Business is New York Citys premier public business school, with an international reputation for excellence in offering nationally-ranked programs, including BBA and MBA (both of which have required and/or elective law courses), specialized MS degrees, and executive programs (including the Executive MBA in Healthcare Administration and a Masters-level concentration in the regulation of financial technology in which the Department of Law faculty teach). Baruch College and The Zicklin School of Business are committed to excellence in research and teaching, and Department of Law faculty publish in top law reviews, attend conferences and share their research regularly. Faculty members are expected to conduct high-quality scholarship and publish their work in prestigious law reviews. Faculty will teach a variety of introductory and advanced business law courses, including courses in Law, Business and Sustainability, and Environmental Law. Other job responsibilities include new course development and service to the Department, School, and College. Applicants should be able to teach in multiple modalities (in-person, online, hybrid) and participate in Zicklin programs offered both on campus and with our global partners. Faculty will join a vibrant, research and teaching focused faculty and work in a supportive, collegial atmosphere. **QUALIFICATIONS** Applicants must have a JD degree or a terminal law degree from an ABA-accredited U.S. law school or be admitted to practice law in the United States and have an excellent academic record. Candidates should have a record of scholarly publication, a rigorous research agenda and be committed to teaching business law at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The Department of Law strongly prefers candidates with expertise in environmental law, law and sustainability, ESG (environmental, social, and governance) regulation, climate law, or related areas of environmental law and sustainability. **COMPENSATION** $135,000$150,000; Compensation and teaching responsibilities will be competitive and commensurate with rank. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** To apply, go to www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Applicants should include a CV, a research statement, and a statement of teaching philosophy that includes, but is not limited to their commitment to and experience with teaching students in a campus environment with a substantial population of students who are among the first-generation of their family to attend a college or university. Candidates invited for an interview will also be required to submit CUNY Application Part 1 and names and contact information for three (3) references prior to the interview. To ensure full consideration, applications must be submitted by October 1, 2026. Please note that documents submitted by e-mail are not a substitute for a CUNY online application all applications must be submitted via the central CUNY application system. **CLOSING DATE** December 8, 2026, with review of resumes to begin October 1, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32627 Location: Baruch College Job Type: Full-Time"
    }
  },
